__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Everything the capture and the logs write. These are the operator's own
# record: the prices they were quoted, the bets they placed, and the stakes
# they placed them at. `git add -A` would sweep the lot into a commit, and
# nothing above this line would have stopped it.
#
# The tracked files under data/ are the example fixtures and the weekly
# slates, which are model output and carry nothing private. They are listed
# back in explicitly rather than left to a narrower pattern, so adding a new
# runtime file defaults to ignored instead of defaulting to committed.
data/*
!data/example_*.csv
!data/week*_slate.csv

# The raw capture and anything derived from it, wherever it is written.
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.gz
capture.log

# The EDGE OS ledger. D3 puts it on the `capture-data` branch, never on main:
# automation appends rows there and code changes here by pull request, and the
# two must not be able to arrive in the same commit. `*.jsonl` above already
# catches the row files; this catches the snapshots, receipts and inbox beside
# them.
#
# Anchored at the root. A bare `ledger/` also matches `cfb_edge/ledger/`,
# which is the writer's own source code, and silently kept it out of a commit.
/ledger/
